\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces Jacobian determinant in the density push-forward formula. A smooth nonlinear diffeomorphism radially compresses the middle of a cropped colored grid and adds a radius-dependent twist. The source density is locally uniform, but the target density, rendered as a blue image with contours of $\rho _\beta $, forms an almost isotropic central bump where the deformed grid cells have smaller area. The target panel is a crop of a larger warped grid, so no artificial square boundary is visible. This illustrates the factor $|\qopname  \relax m{det}T'(x)|^{-1}$ in\nobreakspace  {}\textup  {\hbox {\mathsurround \z@ \normalfont  (\ignorespaces \ref  {eq-pfwd-density}\unskip \@@italiccorr )}}.}}{15}{figure.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:monge-jacobian-pushforward-density}{{2.1}{15}{Jacobian determinant in the density push-forward formula. A smooth nonlinear diffeomorphism radially compresses the middle of a cropped colored grid and adds a radius-dependent twist. The source density is locally uniform, but the target density, rendered as a blue image with contours of $\rho _\be $, forms an almost isotropic central bump where the deformed grid cells have smaller area. The target panel is a crop of a larger warped grid, so no artificial square boundary is visible. This illustrates the factor $|\det \T '(x)|^{-1}$ in~\eqref {eq-pfwd-density}}{figure.2.1}{}}
